HabitFlow — Habit Tracker PRD
1. Product Overview

App name: HabitFlow
Platform: Mobile
Framework: React Native + Expo
Target: iOS & Android
Backend: None for V1
Storage: Local device storage
Authentication: None

Core idea

A simple but polished habit tracker where users can:

Create habits
Track daily completion
Maintain streaks
See weekly/monthly progress
Edit or delete habits
View habit history
Manage basic app settings

The app should feel like a real consumer mobile app, not a demo or developer prototype.

2. Navigation Structure

Use a bottom tab navigation with 3 main tabs:

Home
  ↓
Progress
  ↓
Settings

There should also be a prominent "+" button on the Home screen for creating a habit.

Navigation map
Launch
   ↓
Home
 ┌──────┼─────────┐
 ↓      ↓         ↓
Add    Habit     Progress
Habit  Details      ↓
 ↓       ↓       History
Home    Edit
        Habit

Home
 ↓
Settings
 ├── Appearance
 ├── Notifications
 └── About
3. Screen List
Screen 1 — Launch / Splash
Purpose

Give the app a polished startup experience.

Elements
HabitFlow logo
App name
Short tagline
Simple animation/fade
Automatically transition to Home
Example tagline

Build better days, one habit at a time.

No login or onboarding is required.

4. Screen 2 — Home Dashboard

This is the main screen and most important screen.

Header
Greeting
Current date
Small profile/settings icon

Example:

Good morning 👋
Saturday, September 26

Your habits
Today's Progress

Display:

Completed habits
Total habits
Progress percentage
Circular or horizontal progress indicator

Example:

TODAY'S PROGRESS

      4 / 6
       67%

████████████░░░░
Habit List

Each habit card should contain:

Habit icon
Habit name
Current streak
Today's completion state
Completion button/checkmark

Example:

💧  Drink Water
    🔥 7 day streak                 ✓

📚  Study
    🔥 12 day streak               ○

🏃  Exercise
    🔥 5 day streak                ○
Interactions

Tapping the completion button:

Marks the habit complete
Updates progress
Updates streak
Gives subtle visual feedback

Tapping the habit card:

→ Opens Habit Details

Floating Add Button

A prominent + button:

                +

→ Opens Create Habit

Bottom Navigation
⌂ Home     ◉ Progress     ⚙ Settings
5. Screen 3 — Create Habit

Opened by:

Home → +

Fields
Habit Name

Example:

Read 20 minutes

Icon

Allow user to select from a small collection of icons.

Examples:

📚
💧
🏃
🧘
💪
🥗
🎯
✍️
Color

Allow selection of a few predefined colors.

Frequency

Options:

Every day
Weekdays
Custom

For V1, custom can simply allow selecting individual weekdays.

Bottom Button

Create Habit

After creation:

→ Return to Home

